# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in for a real build, or set
# this in the build environment (e.g. CI/deploy secrets or variables).
# This file defines one variable, GA4's measurement id: leaving it unset
# disables GA4 entirely (src/misc/GoogleAnalytics.ts) rather than falling
# back to a hardcoded id.
#
# Sentry has no variable here - its DSN is hardcoded in src/index.tsx,
# deliberately. A Sentry DSN is public by design: it ships in every
# client bundle and is write-only, good for nothing but sending events
# into that one project. Rotating it is tracked separately, issue #42.

# GA4 measurement id (e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX) for src/misc/GoogleAnalytics.ts.
# Leave unset in dev/test/any build without a real GA4 property - GA4
# then never loads at all. Analytics is initialised with consent denied
# by default (GDPR - the clinic is in the EU) and will report nothing
# until #67 ships a consent banner.
#
# This is a *web data stream* id, not a property id. The owner's decision
# (September 2026) is that icl-calc gets its own new web data stream
# inside the GA4 property that already exists, rather than its own
# property: history, users and cross-site reporting stay in one place,
# while icl-calc's traffic stays identifiable instead of blending into
# another site's numbers. Note the consequence - the *stream* starts
# empty; what is preserved is the property around it. In reports,
# icl-calc is the `ruipinge.github.io` hostname.
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
